# Saved searches: store the query on show under a name, run it in place and in a new tab, pin
# one to a folder and run it from elsewhere, replace one by re-saving its name, rename one, and
# delete one. The run is unindexed, so a this-PC search is saved and listed but not run — that
# is gsearch's rule too.

tree .
refresh

# --- save what the box holds -----------------------------------------------------------
search report
assert-flattened
dialog saved-search
save-search Reports
assert-saved-search Reports
state

# --- run it in place (a template: wherever the tab is) ----------------------------------
clear-search
assert-not-flattened
run-saved Reports
assert-flattened
assert-count 3
assert-status report
shot saved-sidebar

# --- and in a tab of its own -----------------------------------------------------------
run-saved Reports newtab
assert-tabs 2
assert-flattened
assert-count 3
closetab
assert-tabs 1

# --- pinned: saved inside Documents, run from the root, lands in Documents --------------
clear-search
go Documents
search report
save-search Docs reports folder
up
assert-not-flattened
run-saved Docs reports
assert-path Documents
assert-flattened
assert-count 2

# --- this PC: stored and listed; running it needs an index ------------------------------
save-search Everywhere pc
assert-saved-search Everywhere
saved-searches

# --- re-saving a taken name replaces the row rather than adding one ----------------------
clear-search
search ext:md
save-search reports
saved-searches
run-saved Reports
assert-count 3
assert-row draft.md
assert-no-row notes.txt

# --- rename and delete ------------------------------------------------------------------
rename-saved Reports to Markdown
assert-no-saved-search Reports
assert-saved-search Markdown
# The Settings page lists them under the original's headings: name, what it searches, created, last run.
settings saved-searches
shot saved-settings-page
settings close
remove-saved Markdown
assert-no-saved-search Markdown
remove-saved Docs reports
remove-saved Everywhere
shot saved-sidebar-empty

# --- in the title bar instead: dropdowns, the workspace one named after where the window last came from ---
save-workspace Morning
workspaces-placement titlebar
saved-searches-placement titlebar
assert-visible WorkspaceSwitcher
assert-visible SavedSearchSwitcher
assert-hidden WorkspacesList
shot title-switchers TitleBarRoot
menu workspace-switcher title-workspace-menu
assert-menu-item Morning
assert-menu-item Manage workspaces
menu search-switcher title-search-menu
assert-menu-item No saved searches yet
workspaces-placement sidebar
saved-searches-placement sidebar
assert-hidden WorkspaceSwitcher
remove-workspace Morning
assert-not-launched
state
